# Compiled artifacts. `*.c` is here because `wyn build --debug` drops generated C
# next to the .wyn source, and this tree is full of .wyn sources.
*.c
*.out
*.o

# ...but hand-written C test SOURCES have to be tracked. Without this, adding one
# looks like it worked - `git add` says nothing, the suite passes locally off the
# working copy - and the repo ends up with a gate whose test file does not exist.
# tests/run_tests_parallel.sh is the cautionary tale: it reads a tests/test_list.txt
# that was never committed, so it has always executed zero tests while showing a
# green tick. Un-ignore per directory as C tests are added.
!tls/*.c
!schema/*.c
!https/*.c
